          %h3#cuts_of_other_numbers Cuts of other numbers
          %p
            Instead of starting with rational numbers, we could use any
            %span.newWikiWord
              dense
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/dense+suborder"} ?
            subset of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dyadic+number"} dyadic number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            that is still a dense subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            (although you have to know what
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is to state this). For example, we could start with the real
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number"} algebraic number
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computable+number"} computable number
          %p
            The basic theory also generalises immediately to any unbounded,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+linear+order"} dense linear order
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+infinite+set"} countably infinite set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+completion"} Dedekind completion
            for unbounded dense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiorders"} quasiorders
            or unbounded dense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreflexive+comparisons"} irreflexive comparisons
            or Sections 4.31–39 of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HAF"} HAF
            for even more generality.
